{"book":46,"chapter":11,"context":{"chapter":11,"title":"Head Coverings and the Lord's Supper","summary":"Paul addresses head coverings for men and women who pray and prophesy, then rebukes the church for turning the Lord's Supper into a meal that humiliated its poorer members.","background":"In Roman worship men often covered their heads when sacrificing, while customs for women's head coverings varied; how Paul's instructions apply today is debated. Early churches ate the Lord's Supper as part of a full meal in a home. Wealthier members apparently ate and drank first, while poorer members, perhaps slaves who arrived later, went hungry (vv. 21–22).","customs":[{"term":"Received and delivered","verses":"11:23-26","note":"Paul uses the formal language of passing on tradition. His account of Jesus' words over the bread and cup is likely the earliest written account, predating the Gospels."}],"watchFor":["Women praying and prophesying in worship is assumed (v. 5).","'This do in remembrance of me' (vv. 24–25).","The call to examine oneself and discern 'the Lord's body' (vv. 28–29)."],"connections":["Luke 22:19-20","Matthew 26:26-28","Jeremiah 31:31","Genesis 2:21-23"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Μιμηταί","Mimētai","G3402","N-NPM","Imitators"],["μου","mou","G3165","P-1GS","of me"],["γίνεσθε","ginesthe","G1096","V-PNM-2P","do be"],["καθὼς","kathōs","G2531","CONJ","even as"],["κἀγὼ","kagō","G1473","P-1NS + CONJ","I myself also [am]"],["Χριστοῦ","Christou","G5547","N-GSM-T","of Christ"]],"x":[[50003017,50003017,41],[52001006,52001006,37],[49005001,49005002,34],[46004016,46004016,32],[58006012,58006012,32],[50002004,50002005,20],[53003009,53003009,17],[45015002,45015003,8],[46010033,46010033,6]],"xn":9},"2":{"w":[["Ἐπαινῶ","Epainō","G1867","V-PAI-1S","I commend"],["δὲ","de","G1161","CONJ","now"],["ὑμᾶς","humas","G4771","P-2AP","you"],["ἀδελφοί","adelphoi","G80","N-VPM","brothers"],["ὅτι","hoti","G3754","CONJ","that"],["πάντα","panta","G3956","A-APN","in all things"],["μου","mou",